messages.content:
A bitter wind arose, grim-faced and cold;
The world grew sad in snow and frost's stronghold.
The mountains seemed of camphor, white and pale;
The sky was dark, the sun behind a veil.
The gale came roaring out of rock and stone,
Like lions roaring when the horns are blown.
No path was seen, no bird, no beast of prey;
The snow fell endless, night and blinding day.
Such is the world: now harsh and cold its breath,
Now crowns it gives, now fortune dark as death.

Now that you've climbed the chieftain's seat of state,
Guard well your people, small as well as great.
Unstop your ears and listen when they speak;
Show no vain pride, nor scorn the low and meek.
See merit, give reward with open hand;
When someone slips, be slow to draw your brand.
Ride at the front, and let the host come after:
First in the toil, and last in spoils and laughter.
For if you sow with love, then thanks will grow;
Sow hate, and fear is all the field will show.

A cry went up before the royal gate;
The countless host was stirred to march in state.
The drums were beaten and the pipes were blown;
It seemed the mountains trembled, stone on stone.
The shining banner fluttered at the head;
Like Oxus' waves the endless army spread.
The horsemen's dust made all the heavens black;
The earth grew dazed beneath the hooves' attack.
And at the front rode Rostam, vast of frame,
Girt for the road, the host-breaker of fame.

When spring had come, the world was made anew;
Beyond all measure flowers and green grass grew.
The earth became like Eram's garden fair;
With musk the breeze, with joy the desert air.
Upon the bough the nightingale gave song;
The earth wore silk of blossoms all along.
The kings sat down to feast with harp and lute,
With wine in hand, and song, and gathered fruit.
On this, Nowruz, which Jamshid founded first,
Wash grief away, and quench your spirit's thirst.

When anger comes, the div laughs at your deed;
Call wisdom forth, and rein your fiery steed.
Like Kavus, who in wrath lost counsel's aid,
Wronged Rostam, and was left without his blade.
Hold back your breath a moment, and be still;
Then speak, when calm has cleansed your heart and will.
Rage is a tree whose only fruit is grief;
Patience, a herb that brings the wound relief.

Through justice and through bounty, Fereydun rose;
Through Zahhak, all the world was drowned in woes.
The one gave treasure, and won every heart;
The other fed on brains, and fell apart.
The tyrant fears his people in the night;
By day their cries bring terror to his sight.
But he who rules with justice as his creed
Sleeps sound in peace, his land from terror freed.
Know this, young friend: by justice and by love,
The throne is lit with glory from above.

From every treasure, every wage you earn,
Set by a share where thieves shall never learn.
First from your earnings, set your own part free;
Then spend what's left, as far as it may be.
Buy not in haste each thing the market shows;
Wait three days: if desire still stays, then choose.
Keep far from heavy debt, O youthful friend:
For debt puts chains on heroes in the end.
Grain upon grain, a treasure grows a hill;
Weary not of this counsel, man of skill.

Tahmineh, in the night, unlocked her heart
And told the love she'd hidden from the start.
Let shame not hold you: shame keeps love concealed;
A bud that never opens is not revealed.
Speak gently, with a true heart, what you feel;
Press not, but give them room to feel what's real.
If they say "yes," then glad the matter's end;
If they say "no," let no grudge poison, friend.
For hearts are never won by force or might:
Live glad and free, unscarred, with spirit light.

The desert blazed like hell at morning's height;
Its sands threw back the sun's fierce glaring light.
No water, shade, nor leaf, nor fruit to find;
Mirage on every side, and dust on the wind.
The mirage showed a pool, and fooled the eye;
The thirsting lips grew angry, parched and dry.
A caravan moved slowly, worn and weak;
By night the road, by day the shade they'd seek.
When night came down, the stars in heaven shone,
And cold changed all the desert: heat was gone.
